A laboratory technician conducts a redox titration to find the concentration of a potassium ferricyanide (K3[Fe(CN)6]) solution. A 30.00 mL sample of this solution is titrated with 0.0250 M sodium thiosulfate (Na2S2O3). The balanced redox reaction in acidic medium is:

2 Fe(CN)6^{3-} + 3 S2O3^{2-} → 2 Fe(CN)6^{4-} + 3 S4O6^{2-}

If 22.50 mL of the sodium thiosulfate solution is required to reach the endpoint, what is the molarity of the potassium ferricyanide solution? Assume the endpoint is detected accurately by the disappearance of the solution's color.
